{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "ws_0b97e77e51b7b4ea016a85ded5f9208191969618eb6ad15cba", "rollout_ordinal": 1116, "created_at_ms": 1787158248257, "item_type": "webSearch", "updated_at_ordinal": 1116, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "webSearch", "id": "ws_0b97e77e51b7b4ea016a85ded5f9208191969618eb6ad15cba", "query": "Qt for Python PySide6 official documentation QML desktop applications", "action": {"type": "search", "query": "Qt for Python PySide6 official documentation QML desktop applications", "queries": ["Qt for Python PySide6 official documentation QML desktop applications", "pywebview official documentation Python webview desktop GUI", "Tauri official documentation sidecar command desktop app", "Electron official documentation desktop app"]}, "results": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-175", "rollout_ordinal": 1118, "created_at_ms": 1787158270054, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1119, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-175", "summary": ["**Planning pywebview desktop wrapper**", "**Confirming pywebview installation feasibility**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-176", "rollout_ordinal": 1121, "created_at_ms": 1787158270157, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1121, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-176", "text": "Sí, hay manera, y de hecho el camino más directo para mantener ese estilo Live como app de escritorio es envolver la UI web en una ventana nativa. Voy a dejar una prueba de escritorio con `pywebview`: se ve como app moderna, pero sigue pudiendo llamar backend Python.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-177", "rollout_ordinal": 1124, "created_at_ms": 1787158271489, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1124, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-177", "text": "Voy a comprobar si `pywebview` está disponible en el entorno compatible de Python 3.10; si no, lo instalaré dentro del `venv\\Lib\\site-packages` igual que hicimos con `sounddevice`.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-178", "rollout_ordinal": 1131, "created_at_ms": 1787158276404, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1131, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-178", "text": "No está instalado todavía, así que lo agrego al entorno compatible. Después creo el lanzador de escritorio y una API Python mínima para demostrar cómo se comunicaría la UI con el backend.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-179", "rollout_ordinal": 1136, "created_at_ms": 1787158302415, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1137, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-179", "summary": ["**Planning desktop_live.py with pywebview integration**", "**Designing song data loading with downsampling**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-180", "rollout_ordinal": 1139, "created_at_ms": 1787158303336, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1139, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-180", "text": "La instalacion quedó lista. Ahora creo `desktop_live.py`: abre `ui_live/index.html` en una ventana de escritorio y expone una API Python mínima para cargar canciones reales del catálogo cuando existan.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "call_xQQr06BgpO7NAmeLHTYJByLd", "rollout_ordinal": 1142, "created_at_ms": 1787158314833, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1142, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_xQQr06BgpO7NAmeLHTYJByLd", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\desktop_live.py", "kind": {"type": "add"}, "diff": "import os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport soundfile as sf\nimport webview\n\nfrom audio.catalogo import cargar_canciones, leer_pitch_csv\nfrom audio.metricas import hz_to_midi\n\n\nclass LiveBackend:\n    def get_songs(self):\n        canciones = []\n        for cancion in cargar_canciones():\n            canciones.append(\n                {\n                    \"id\": cancion[\"id\"],\n                    \"title\": cancion.get(\"titulo\", \"Sin titulo\"),\n                    \"artist\": cancion.get(\"artista\") or \"Sin artista\",\n                    \"duration\": self._duracion_cancion(cancion),\n                    \"prepared\": bool(cancion.get(\"preparada\")),\n                    \"points\": self._puntos_referencia(cancion),\n                }\n            )\n        return canciones\n\n    def get_status(self):\n        return {\n            \"backend\": \"Python\",\n            \"ui\": \"pywebview\",\n            \"ready\": True,\n        }\n\n    def _duracion_cancion(self, cancion):\n        for key in [\"instrumental\", \"original\", \"vocals\"]:\n            ruta = cancion.get(key)\n            if ruta and os.path.exists(ruta):\n                try:\n                    return float(sf.info(ruta).duration)\n                except RuntimeError:\n                    continue\n        return 0\n\n    def _puntos_referencia(self, cancion):\n        ruta = cancion.get(\"pitch_referencia\")\n        if not ruta or not os.path.exists(ruta):\n            return []\n\n        tiempos, frecuencias = leer_pitch_csv(ruta)\n        midi = hz_to_midi(frecuencias)\n        puntos = [\n            [float(t), float(m)]\n            for t, m in zip(tiempos, midi)\n            if not np.isnan(m)\n        ]\n        return self._reducir_puntos(puntos)\n\n    def _reducir_puntos(self, puntos, max_puntos=900):\n        if len(puntos) <= max_puntos:\n            return puntos\n        salto = max(1, len(puntos) // max_puntos)\n        return puntos[::salto]\n\n\ndef main():\n    html_path = Path(__file__).parent / \"ui_live\" / \"index.html\"\n    window = webview.create_window(\n        \"Karaoke Live\",\n        html_path.resolve().as_uri(),\n        js_api=LiveBackend(),\n        width=1280,\n        height=820,\n        min_size=(980, 620),\n    )\n    webview.start(debug=False)\n    return window\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-181", "rollout_ordinal": 1145, "created_at_ms": 1787158317364, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1145, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-181", "text": "Ahora creo el `.bat` para abrir esa versión como app de escritorio con Python 3.10 y el entorno compatible.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "call_QDuDeSg64yxe1QWJ25BeCu3P", "rollout_ordinal": 1148, "created_at_ms": 1787158318727, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1148, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_QDuDeSg64yxe1QWJ25BeCu3P", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\iniciar_live.bat", "kind": {"type": "add"}, "diff": "@echo off\nsetlocal\ncd /d \"%~dp0\"\nset \"PYTHONPATH=%CD%\\venv\\Lib\\site-packages\"\npy -3.10 desktop_live.py\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-182", "rollout_ordinal": 1151, "created_at_ms": 1787158322643, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1151, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-182", "text": "Voy a adaptar el JS para que, si corre dentro de pywebview, cargue canciones reales desde Python; si se abre en navegador común, mantiene datos simulados.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "call_nRd3wGBn0112MU5Di1NQyRMf", "rollout_ordinal": 1154, "created_at_ms": 1787158328553, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1154, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_nRd3wGBn0112MU5Di1NQyRMf", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\ui_live\\app.js", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@\n-const songs = [\n+const mockSongs = [\n   {\n@@ -37,2 +37,4 @@\n \n+let songs = [...mockSongs];\n+\n const state = {\n@@ -80,2 +82,33 @@\n \n+function normalizeBackendSongs(backendSongs) {\n+  if (!Array.isArray(backendSongs) || backendSongs.length === 0) {\n+    return mockSongs;\n+  }\n+\n+  return backendSongs.map((song) => ({\n+    title: song.title || \"Sin titulo\",\n+    artist: song.artist || \"Sin artista\",\n+    duration: Number(song.duration || 0),\n+    prepared: Boolean(song.prepared),\n+    points: Array.isArray(song.points) && song.points.length ? song.points : [[0, 60], [1, 60]]\n+  }));\n+}\n+\n+async function loadBackendSongs() {\n+  if (!window.pywebview?.api?.get_songs) {\n+    return;\n+  }\n+\n+  try {\n+    songs = normalizeBackendSongs(await window.pywebview.api.get_songs());\n+    state.selectedIndex = 0;\n+    state.current = 0;\n+    renderSongs();\n+    updateSongLabels();\n+    renderChart();\n+  } catch (error) {\n+    console.warn(\"No se pudo cargar el catalogo desde Python\", error);\n+  }\n+}\n+\n function renderSongs() {\n@@ -351 +384,3 @@\n renderChart();\n+\n+window.addEventListener(\"pywebviewready\", loadBackendSongs);\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-183", "rollout_ordinal": 1157, "created_at_ms": 1787158335900, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1157, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-183", "text": "Voy a verificar imports en Python 3.10 y sintaxis del JS. No abriré la ventana desde aquí porque una app de escritorio puede quedar corriendo hasta que alguien la cierre.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-184", "rollout_ordinal": 1166, "created_at_ms": 1787158348699, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1166, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-184", "summary": ["**Summarizing pywebview features and alternatives**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01aee-406e-75f2-8bd5-5a0eb9d8dae6", "item_id": "item-185", "rollout_ordinal": 1168, "created_at_ms": 1787158358246, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1168, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-185", "text": "Sí, se puede perfectamente. Para tu caso, la mejor ruta es **mantener una interfaz web moderna como Live, pero ejecutarla dentro de una app de escritorio**.\n\nYa dejé una primera prueba de escritorio con **pywebview**:\n\n- [desktop_live.py](<C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke/desktop_live.py>)\n- [iniciar_live.bat](<C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke/iniciar_live.bat>)\n- [ui_live/index.html](<C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke/ui_live/index.html>)\n- [ui_live/styles.css](<C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke/ui_live/styles.css>)\n- [ui_live/app.js](<C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke/ui_live/app.js>)\n\nPuedes probarla con:\n\n```powershell\n.\\iniciar_live.bat\n```\n\nEsto abre la UI estilo **Live** como ventana de escritorio, no como Tkinter. Además ya dejé una API Python inicial para que la interfaz pueda leer canciones reales del catálogo.\n\nLa opción que recomiendo para tu proyecto es:\n\n**Frontend:** HTML/CSS/JS estilo `ui_live`  \n**Contenedor desktop:** `pywebview`  \n**Backend:** Python 3.10 con tus módulos de audio, Demucs, pitch, métricas y comparación\n\nVentajas:\n\n- Se ve moderno.\n- Sigue siendo aplicación de escritorio.\n- Puedes conservar Python para el procesamiento pesado.\n- No obliga a reescribir todo en JavaScript.\n- Es mucho más flexible visualmente que Tkinter.\n\nOtras opciones posibles:\n\n- **PySide6/QML:** muy buena para apps nativas modernas, pero habría que rehacer más interfaz.\n- **Electron:** muy potente, pero más pesado.\n- **Tauri:** más liviano que Electron, pero requiere más arquitectura y normalmente usar Python como proceso externo/sidecar.\n\nVerifiqué que `pywebview` carga en Python 3.10 y que el JS no tiene errores de sintaxis.\n\nFuentes: [pywebview](https://pywebview.flowrl.com/), [Qt for Python](https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/index.html), [Electron](https://electronjs.org/docs/latest/), [Tauri sidecars](https://v2.tauri.app/develop/sidecar/).", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af2-aadd-7380-a1f7-12f98285e336", "item_id": "item-186", "rollout_ordinal": 1176, "created_at_ms": 1787158506441, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1176, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-186", "clientId": "a87159b9-696d-4d84-8ad2-8bf3f69fe091", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "entonces ahora como lo inicio?\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af2-aadd-7380-a1f7-12f98285e336", "item_id": "item-187", "rollout_ordinal": 1177, "created_at_ms": 1787158509976, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1177, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-187", "text": "Inícialo con este archivo nuevo:\n\n```powershell\n.\\iniciar_live.bat\n```\n\nDesde esta carpeta:\n\n```powershell\nC:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\n```\n\nEso abre la versión de escritorio con estilo **Live** usando Python 3.10 + el entorno del proyecto.\n\nSi quieres volver a la app Tkinter anterior:\n\n```powershell\n.\\iniciar_app.bat\n```", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-188", "rollout_ordinal": 1185, "created_at_ms": 1787158890939, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1185, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-188", "clientId": "8af40e27-4c98-4c30-b0d6-59d953e45cc7", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "verifica la lógica del nuevo codigo, no se reproduce la música ni se toma correctamente el input del usuario, pareciera ser que toma como imitación de la referencia, no está captando el microfono\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-189", "rollout_ordinal": 1186, "created_at_ms": 1787158897968, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1186, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-189", "summary": ["**Inspecting audio input logic**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-190", "rollout_ordinal": 1188, "created_at_ms": 1787158904522, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1188, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-190", "text": "Sí, tu diagnóstico es correcto: la versión `Live` que dejé era todavía una maqueta conectada solo al catálogo, y la curva roja se estaba simulando a partir de la referencia. Voy a convertirla en flujo real: reproducir instrumental, grabar micrófono y enviar pitch real desde Python hacia la UI.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-191", "rollout_ordinal": 1199, "created_at_ms": 1787158966575, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1204, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-191", "summary": ["**Planning backend integration for live recording**", "**Designing polling-based backend-to-frontend syncing**", "**Outlining LiveBackend class and session methods**", "**Implementing session result handling and UI polling**", "**Refining UI for session results and no-song handling**", "**Finalizing session control flow and UI state management**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-192", "rollout_ordinal": 1206, "created_at_ms": 1787158968008, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1206, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-192", "text": "El problema principal está confirmado: `ui_live/app.js` todavía tenía `appendMockUserPoint()`, que fabricaba la línea roja desde la referencia. Ahora voy a reemplazar esa simulación por llamadas reales a `desktop_live.py`: iniciar sesión, detener sesión, consultar progreso y recibir puntos de pitch reales.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_ihMjhRVh9jNGMalXRZghuMG4", "rollout_ordinal": 1209, "created_at_ms": 1787158996099, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1209, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_ihMjhRVh9jNGMalXRZghuMG4", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\desktop_live.py", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -1,2 +1,3 @@\n import os\n+import threading\n from pathlib import Path\n@@ -7,3 +8,4 @@\n \n-from audio.catalogo import cargar_canciones, leer_pitch_csv\n+from audio.catalogo import cargar_cancion, cargar_canciones, leer_pitch_csv\n+from audio.karaoke import comparar_grabacion, grabar_con_instrumental\n from audio.metricas import hz_to_midi\n@@ -12,2 +14,20 @@\n class LiveBackend:\n+    def __init__(self):\n+        self._lock = threading.Lock()\n+        self._detener = threading.Event()\n+        self._hilo = None\n+        self._pitch_pendiente = []\n+        self._estado = self._estado_inicial()\n+\n+    def _estado_inicial(self):\n+        return {\n+            \"status\": \"idle\",\n+            \"current\": 0.0,\n+            \"duration\": 0.0,\n+            \"song_id\": None,\n+            \"recording_path\": None,\n+            \"result\": None,\n+            \"error\": None,\n+        }\n+\n     def get_songs(self):\n@@ -27,2 +47,51 @@\n \n+    def start_session(self, song_id):\n+        with self._lock:\n+            if self._estado[\"status\"] in [\"recording\", \"comparing\"]:\n+                return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"Ya hay una grabacion en curso.\"}\n+\n+        try:\n+            cancion = cargar_cancion(song_id)\n+            if not cancion.get(\"preparada\"):\n+                return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"La cancion no esta preparada.\"}\n+            if not os.path.exists(cancion.get(\"instrumental\", \"\")):\n+                return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"No existe la pista instrumental.\"}\n+        except Exception as exc:\n+            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": str(exc)}\n+\n+        self._detener.clear()\n+        with self._lock:\n+            self._pitch_pendiente = []\n+            self._estado = {\n+                \"status\": \"recording\",\n+                \"current\": 0.0,\n+                \"duration\": self._duracion_cancion(cancion),\n+                \"song_id\": song_id,\n+                \"recording_path\": None,\n+                \"result\": None,\n+                \"error\": None,\n+            }\n+\n+        self._hilo = threading.Thread(\n+            target=self._ejecutar_sesion,\n+            args=(cancion,),\n+            daemon=True,\n+        )\n+        self._hilo.start()\n+        return {\"ok\": True, \"state\": self.get_session_state()}\n+\n+    def stop_session(self):\n+        self._detener.set()\n+        with self._lock:\n+            if self._estado[\"status\"] == \"recording\":\n+                self._estado[\"status\"] = \"stopping\"\n+        return {\"ok\": True}\n+\n+    def get_session_state(self):\n+        with self._lock:\n+            estado = dict(self._estado)\n+            estado[\"pitch_points\"] = list(self._pitch_pendiente)\n+            self._pitch_pendiente = []\n+        return estado\n+\n     def get_status(self):\n@@ -34,2 +103,75 @@\n \n+    def _ejecutar_sesion(self, cancion):\n+        try:\n+            ruta_grabacion = grabar_con_instrumental(\n+                cancion,\n+                detener_evento=self._detener,\n+                progreso_callback=self._actualizar_progreso,\n+                pitch_callback=self._agregar_pitch_usuario,\n+                intervalo_pitch=0.1,\n+                segundos_chunk_pitch=0.7,\n+            )\n+\n+            with self._lock:\n+                self._estado[\"status\"] = \"comparing\"\n+                self._estado[\"recording_path\"] = ruta_grabacion\n+\n+            resultado = comparar_grabacion(cancion, ruta_grabacion)\n+            resultado_ui = self._resultado_para_ui(resultado)\n+\n+            with self._lock:\n+                self._estado[\"status\"] = \"finished\"\n+                self._estado[\"result\"] = resultado_ui\n+        except Exception as exc:\n+            with self._lock:\n+                self._estado[\"status\"] = \"error\"\n+                self._estado[\"error\"] = str(exc)\n+\n+    def _actualizar_progreso(self, tiempo):\n+        with self._lock:\n+            self._estado[\"current\"] = float(tiempo)\n+            if self._estado[\"status\"] == \"stopping\":\n+                self._estado[\"status\"] = \"recording\"\n+\n+    def _agregar_pitch_usuario(self, tiempos, frecuencias):\n+        midi = hz_to_midi(frecuencias)\n+        puntos = [\n+            [float(t), float(m)]\n+            for t, m in zip(tiempos, midi)\n+            if not np.isnan(m)\n+        ]\n+        with self._lock:\n+            self._pitch_pendiente.extend(puntos)\n+            if len(self._pitch_pendiente) > 300:\n+                self._pitch_pendiente = self._pitch_pendiente[-300:]\n+\n+    def _resultado_para_ui(self, resultado):\n+        grafico = resultado.get(\"grafico\") or {}\n+        salida = {\n+            \"error_prom\": resultado.get(\"error_prom\"),\n+            \"desviacion\": resultado.get(\"desviacion\"),\n+            \"tendencia\": resultado.get(\"tendencia\"),\n+            \"porcentaje_50\": resultado.get(\"porcentaje_50\"),\n+            \"porcentaje_100\": resultado.get(\"porcentaje_100\"),\n+            \"puntos_comparados\": resultado.get(\"puntos_comparados\"),\n+            \"mensaje\": resultado.get(\"mensaje\"),\n+            \"points_ref\": self._puntos_hz_a_midi(\n+                grafico.get(\"t_ref\", []),\n+                grafico.get(\"f_ref\", []),\n+            ),\n+            \"points_user\": self._puntos_hz_a_midi(\n+                grafico.get(\"t_usr\", []),\n+                grafico.get(\"f_usr\", []),\n+            ),\n+        }\n+        return salida\n+\n+    def _puntos_hz_a_midi(self, tiempos, frecuencias):\n+        midi = hz_to_midi(frecuencias)\n+        return [\n+            [float(t), float(m)]\n+            for t, m in zip(tiempos, midi)\n+            if not np.isnan(m)\n+        ]\n+\n     def _duracion_cancion(self, cancion):\n@@ -66,3 +208,5 @@\n def main():\n+    os.chdir(Path(__file__).parent)\n     html_path = Path(__file__).parent / \"ui_live\" / \"index.html\"\n+    backend = LiveBackend()\n     window = webview.create_window(\n@@ -70,3 +214,3 @@\n         html_path.resolve().as_uri(),\n-        js_api=LiveBackend(),\n+        js_api=backend,\n         width=1280,\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-193", "rollout_ordinal": 1213, "created_at_ms": 1787159002005, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1213, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-193", "text": "Ya hay backend real para iniciar/detener sesión. Ahora reemplazo el JS para que en modo escritorio no simule nada: el botón `Cantar` llama a Python, `Detener` corta la grabación, y la curva roja llega desde el micrófono vía polling al backend.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_c10x4S5sLIv8UwQKz0bOsevO", "rollout_ordinal": 1216, "created_at_ms": 1787159002442, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1216, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_c10x4S5sLIv8UwQKz0bOsevO", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\ui_live\\app.js", "kind": {"type": "delete"}, "diff": "const mockSongs = [\n  {\n    title: \"Contigo en la distancia\",\n    artist: \"Luis Miguel\",\n    duration: 192,\n    prepared: true,\n    points: [\n      [0, 61], [8, 61], [12, 65], [20, 65], [25, 63], [32, 63],\n      [38, 67], [48, 67], [54, 65], [64, 65], [72, 69], [82, 69],\n      [90, 67], [100, 67], [110, 71], [121, 71], [130, 68], [142, 68],\n      [152, 65], [164, 65], [174, 63], [190, 63]\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    title: \"La incondicional\",\n    artist: \"Luis Miguel\",\n    duration: 240,\n    prepared: true,\n    points: [\n      [0, 59], [12, 59], [18, 62], [30, 62], [38, 66], [52, 66],\n      [64, 64], [78, 64], [92, 67], [110, 67], [128, 69], [146, 69],\n      [160, 66], [178, 66], [196, 64], [226, 64]\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    title: \"Nada fue un error\",\n    artist: \"Coti\",\n    duration: 214,\n    prepared: false,\n    points: [\n      [0, 57], [14, 57], [22, 60], [36, 60], [48, 62], [66, 62],\n      [82, 64], [98, 64], [112, 62], [130, 62], [146, 65], [168, 65],\n      [184, 62], [210, 62]\n    ]\n  }\n];\n\nlet songs = [...mockSongs];\n\nconst state = {\n  selectedIndex: 0,\n  playing: false,\n  detail: false,\n  current: 0,\n  viewStart: 0,\n  viewWindow: 12,\n  yMin: 57,\n  yMax: 72,\n  userPoints: [],\n  animationId: null,\n  lastFrame: null\n};\n\nconst els = {\n  songList: document.getElementById(\"songList\"),\n  artistLabel: document.getElementById(\"artistLabel\"),\n  songTitle: document.getElementById(\"songTitle\"),\n  statusDot: document.getElementById(\"statusDot\"),\n  statusLabel: document.getElementById(\"statusLabel\"),\n  currentTime: document.getElementById(\"currentTime\"),\n  durationTime: document.getElementById(\"durationTime\"),\n  currentNote: document.getElementById(\"currentNote\"),\n  mockError: document.getElementById(\"mockError\"),\n  chartShell: document.getElementById(\"chartShell\"),\n  noteRuler: document.getElementById(\"noteRuler\"),\n  gridLayer: document.getElementById(\"gridLayer\"),\n  referencePath: document.getElementById(\"referencePath\"),\n  userPath: document.getElementById(\"userPath\"),\n  cursorLine: document.getElementById(\"cursorLine\"),\n  timelineFill: document.getElementById(\"timelineFill\"),\n  startButton: document.getElementById(\"startButton\"),\n  stopButton: document.getElementById(\"stopButton\"),\n  detailButton: document.getElementById(\"detailButton\"),\n  fullButton: document.getElementById(\"fullButton\"),\n  detailX: document.getElementById(\"detailX\"),\n  detailY: document.getElementById(\"detailY\"),\n  metricTight: document.getElementById(\"metricTight\"),\n  metricLoose: document.getElementById(\"metricLoose\"),\n  metricTrend: document.getElementById(\"metricTrend\"),\n  metricPoints: document.getElementById(\"metricPoints\")\n};\n\nfunction normalizeBackendSongs(backendSongs) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(backendSongs) || backendSongs.length === 0) {\n    return mockSongs;\n  }\n\n  return backendSongs.map((song) => ({\n    title: song.title || \"Sin titulo\",\n    artist: song.artist || \"Sin artista\",\n    duration: Number(song.duration || 0),\n    prepared: Boolean(song.prepared),\n    points: Array.isArray(song.points) && song.points.length ? song.points : [[0, 60], [1, 60]]\n  }));\n}\n\nasync function loadBackendSongs() {\n  if (!window.pywebview?.api?.get_songs) {\n    return;\n  }\n\n  try {\n    songs = normalizeBackendSongs(await window.pywebview.api.get_songs());\n    state.selectedIndex = 0;\n    state.current = 0;\n    renderSongs();\n    updateSongLabels();\n    renderChart();\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.warn(\"No se pudo cargar el catalogo desde Python\", error);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderSongs() {\n  els.songList.innerHTML = \"\";\n  songs.forEach((song, index) => {\n    const button = document.createElement(\"button\");\n    button.className = `song-card${index === state.selectedIndex ? \" is-active\" : \"\"}`;\n    button.type = \"button\";\n    button.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"song-title\">${song.title}</div>\n      <div class=\"song-artist\">${song.artist}</div>\n      <div class=\"song-meta\">\n        <span>${formatTime(song.duration)}</span>\n        <span>${song.prepared ? \"Lista\" : \"Sin procesar\"}</span>\n      </div>\n    `;\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () => selectSong(index));\n    els.songList.appendChild(button);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction selectSong(index) {\n  stopPlayback();\n  state.selectedIndex = index;\n  state.current = 0;\n  state.viewStart = 0;\n  state.detail = false;\n  state.userPoints = [];\n  updateSongLabels();\n  renderSongs();\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nfunction updateSongLabels() {\n  const song = currentSong();\n  els.artistLabel.textContent = song.artist;\n  els.songTitle.textContent = song.title;\n  els.durationTime.textContent = formatTime(song.duration);\n  els.currentTime.textContent = formatTime(state.current);\n  els.currentNote.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.mockError.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricTight.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricLoose.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricTrend.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricPoints.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.statusLabel.textContent = \"Listo\";\n  els.statusDot.classList.remove(\"is-recording\");\n  els.startButton.disabled = !song.prepared;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n  els.detailButton.disabled = true;\n  els.fullButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  els.chartShell.classList.remove(\"is-detail\");\n}\n\nfunction currentSong() {\n  return songs[state.selectedIndex];\n}\n\nfunction formatTime(seconds) {\n  const minutes = Math.floor(seconds / 60);\n  const rest = Math.floor(seconds % 60).toString().padStart(2, \"0\");\n  return `${minutes}:${rest}`;\n}\n\nfunction noteName(midi) {\n  const names = [\"C\", \"C#\", \"D\", \"D#\", \"E\", \"F\", \"F#\", \"G\", \"G#\", \"A\", \"A#\", \"B\"];\n  const rounded = Math.round(midi);\n  return `${names[((rounded % 12) + 12) % 12]}${Math.floor(rounded / 12) - 1}`;\n}\n\nfunction xScale(time) {\n  const min = state.detail ? state.viewStart : Math.max(0, state.current - state.viewWindow * 0.4);\n  const max = min + state.viewWindow;\n  return 70 + ((time - min) / (max - min)) * 1080;\n}\n\nfunction yScale(midi) {\n  return 486 - ((midi - state.yMin) / (state.yMax - state.yMin)) * 430;\n}\n\nfunction visibleDomain() {\n  const song = currentSong();\n  if (state.detail) {\n    return {\n      xMin: state.viewStart,\n      xMax: state.viewStart + state.viewWindow\n    };\n  }\n  const xMin = Math.max(0, Math.min(song.duration - state.viewWindow, state.current - state.viewWindow * 0.4));\n  return {\n    xMin,\n    xMax: xMin + state.viewWindow\n  };\n}\n\nfunction updateYDomain() {\n  if (state.detail) {\n    const center = Number(els.detailY.value);\n    state.yMin = center - 7;\n    state.yMax = center + 7;\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const domain = visibleDomain();\n  const values = [];\n  currentSong().points.forEach(([time, midi]) => {\n    if (time >= domain.xMin && time <= domain.xMax) values.push(midi);\n  });\n  state.userPoints.forEach(([time, midi]) => {\n    if (time >= domain.xMin && time <= domain.xMax) values.push(midi);\n  });\n  const center = values.length ? median(values) : 64;\n  const min = values.length ? Math.min(...values, center - 5) : center - 5;\n  const max = values.length ? Math.max(...values, center + 5) : center + 5;\n  state.yMin = Math.floor(min) - 1;\n  state.yMax = Math.ceil(max) + 1;\n}\n\nfunction median(values) {\n  const sorted = [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  return sorted[Math.floor(sorted.length / 2)];\n}\n\nfunction buildPath(points) {\n  const domain = visibleDomain();\n  const visible = points.filter(([time]) => time >= domain.xMin - 0.4 && time <= domain.xMax + 0.4);\n  if (!visible.length) return \"\";\n\n  return visible\n    .map(([time, midi], index) => `${index === 0 ? \"M\" : \"L\"} ${xScale(time).toFixed(1)} ${yScale(midi).toFixed(1)}`)\n    .join(\" \");\n}\n\nfunction renderGrid() {\n  els.gridLayer.innerHTML = \"\";\n  els.noteRuler.innerHTML = \"\";\n  for (let midi = Math.ceil(state.yMin); midi <= Math.floor(state.yMax); midi += 1) {\n    const y = yScale(midi);\n    const line = document.createElementNS(\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\", \"line\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"class\", \"grid-line\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"x1\", \"54\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"x2\", \"1200\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"y1\", y);\n    line.setAttribute(\"y2\", y);\n    els.gridLayer.appendChild(line);\n\n    const label = document.createElement(\"span\");\n    label.textContent = noteName(midi);\n    els.noteRuler.appendChild(label);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderChart() {\n  updateYDomain();\n  renderGrid();\n  els.referencePath.setAttribute(\"d\", buildPath(currentSong().points));\n  els.userPath.setAttribute(\"d\", buildPath(state.userPoints));\n  const cursorX = xScale(state.current);\n  els.cursorLine.setAttribute(\"x1\", cursorX);\n  els.cursorLine.setAttribute(\"x2\", cursorX);\n  els.currentTime.textContent = formatTime(state.current);\n  els.timelineFill.style.width = `${Math.min(100, (state.current / currentSong().duration) * 100)}%`;\n}\n\nfunction startPlayback() {\n  state.playing = true;\n  state.detail = false;\n  state.current = 0;\n  state.viewStart = 0;\n  state.userPoints = [];\n  state.lastFrame = null;\n  els.statusLabel.textContent = \"Grabando\";\n  els.statusDot.classList.add(\"is-recording\");\n  els.startButton.disabled = true;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = false;\n  els.detailButton.disabled = true;\n  els.fullButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  els.chartShell.classList.remove(\"is-detail\");\n  loop();\n}\n\nfunction stopPlayback() {\n  if (state.animationId) {\n    cancelAnimationFrame(state.animationId);\n    state.animationId = null;\n  }\n  if (!state.playing) return;\n  state.playing = false;\n  els.statusLabel.textContent = \"Comparacion lista\";\n  els.statusDot.classList.remove(\"is-recording\");\n  els.startButton.disabled = false;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n  els.detailButton.disabled = false;\n  els.mockError.textContent = \"42c\";\n  els.metricTight.textContent = \"71%\";\n  els.metricLoose.textContent = \"91%\";\n  els.metricTrend.textContent = \"Estable\";\n  els.metricPoints.textContent = state.userPoints.length.toString();\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nfunction loop(timestamp = 0) {\n  if (!state.playing) return;\n  if (state.lastFrame == null) state.lastFrame = timestamp;\n  const delta = Math.min(0.08, (timestamp - state.lastFrame) / 1000);\n  state.lastFrame = timestamp;\n  state.current = Math.min(currentSong().duration, state.current + delta);\n  appendMockUserPoint();\n  renderChart();\n\n  if (state.current >= currentSong().duration) {\n    stopPlayback();\n    return;\n  }\n  state.animationId = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n}\n\nfunction appendMockUserPoint() {\n  const song = currentSong();\n  const nearest = nearestReference(song.points, state.current);\n  const vibrato = Math.sin(state.current * 5.4) * 0.25;\n  const drift = Math.sin(state.current * 0.5) * 0.45;\n  const midi = nearest + vibrato + drift;\n  const last = state.userPoints[state.userPoints.length - 1];\n  if (!last || state.current - last[0] >= 0.1) {\n    state.userPoints.push([state.current, midi]);\n    els.currentNote.textContent = noteName(midi);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction nearestReference(points, time) {\n  let nearest = points[0][1];\n  for (const [pointTime, midi] of points) {\n    if (pointTime <= time) nearest = midi;\n    else break;\n  }\n  return nearest;\n}\n\nfunction showDetail() {\n  state.detail = true;\n  const song = currentSong();\n  els.chartShell.classList.add(\"is-detail\");\n  els.detailButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  els.fullButton.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\n  els.detailX.max = Math.max(0, song.duration - state.viewWindow);\n  els.detailX.value = Math.max(0, Math.min(Number(els.detailX.max), state.current - state.viewWindow / 2));\n  els.detailY.value = Math.round((state.yMin + state.yMax) / 2);\n  state.viewStart = Number(els.detailX.value);\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nfunction showFull() {\n  state.detail = false;\n  els.chartShell.classList.remove(\"is-detail\");\n  els.detailButton.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\n  els.fullButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nels.startButton.addEventListener(\"click\", startPlayback);\nels.stopButton.addEventListener(\"click\", stopPlayback);\nels.detailButton.addEventListener(\"click\", showDetail);\nels.fullButton.addEventListener(\"click\", showFull);\nels.detailX.addEventListener(\"input\", () => {\n  state.viewStart = Number(els.detailX.value);\n  renderChart();\n});\nels.detailY.addEventListener(\"input\", renderChart);\n\nrenderSongs();\nupdateSongLabels();\nrenderChart();\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"pywebviewready\", loadBackendSongs);\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_QZIj4ABIW3HjWlhA7r1CgJbF", "rollout_ordinal": 1220, "created_at_ms": 1787159096344, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1220, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_QZIj4ABIW3HjWlhA7r1CgJbF", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\ui_live\\app.js", "kind": {"type": "add"}, "diff": "const mockSongs = [\n  {\n    id: \"mock-1\",\n    title: \"Contigo en la distancia\",\n    artist: \"Luis Miguel\",\n    duration: 192,\n    prepared: true,\n    points: [\n      [0, 61], [8, 61], [12, 65], [20, 65], [25, 63], [32, 63],\n      [38, 67], [48, 67], [54, 65], [64, 65], [72, 69], [82, 69],\n      [90, 67], [100, 67], [110, 71], [121, 71], [130, 68], [142, 68],\n      [152, 65], [164, 65], [174, 63], [190, 63]\n    ]\n  }\n];\n\nlet songs = [...mockSongs];\nlet backendReady = false;\n\nconst state = {\n  selectedIndex: 0,\n  playing: false,\n  detail: false,\n  current: 0,\n  viewStart: 0,\n  viewWindow: 12,\n  yMin: 57,\n  yMax: 72,\n  userPoints: [],\n  animationId: null,\n  pollId: null,\n  sessionStartedAt: null,\n  backendCurrent: 0,\n  backendPollAt: null,\n  lastFrame: null\n};\n\nconst els = {\n  songList: document.getElementById(\"songList\"),\n  artistLabel: document.getElementById(\"artistLabel\"),\n  songTitle: document.getElementById(\"songTitle\"),\n  statusDot: document.getElementById(\"statusDot\"),\n  statusLabel: document.getElementById(\"statusLabel\"),\n  currentTime: document.getElementById(\"currentTime\"),\n  durationTime: document.getElementById(\"durationTime\"),\n  currentNote: document.getElementById(\"currentNote\"),\n  mockError: document.getElementById(\"mockError\"),\n  chartShell: document.getElementById(\"chartShell\"),\n  noteRuler: document.getElementById(\"noteRuler\"),\n  gridLayer: document.getElementById(\"gridLayer\"),\n  referencePath: document.getElementById(\"referencePath\"),\n  userPath: document.getElementById(\"userPath\"),\n  cursorLine: document.getElementById(\"cursorLine\"),\n  timelineFill: document.getElementById(\"timelineFill\"),\n  startButton: document.getElementById(\"startButton\"),\n  stopButton: document.getElementById(\"stopButton\"),\n  detailButton: document.getElementById(\"detailButton\"),\n  fullButton: document.getElementById(\"fullButton\"),\n  detailX: document.getElementById(\"detailX\"),\n  detailY: document.getElementById(\"detailY\"),\n  metricTight: document.getElementById(\"metricTight\"),\n  metricLoose: document.getElementById(\"metricLoose\"),\n  metricTrend: document.getElementById(\"metricTrend\"),\n  metricPoints: document.getElementById(\"metricPoints\")\n};\n\nfunction normalizeBackendSongs(backendSongs) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(backendSongs)) return [];\n  return backendSongs.map((song) => ({\n    id: song.id,\n    title: song.title || \"Sin titulo\",\n    artist: song.artist || \"Sin artista\",\n    duration: Number(song.duration || 0),\n    prepared: Boolean(song.prepared),\n    points: Array.isArray(song.points) ? song.points : []\n  }));\n}\n\nasync function loadBackendSongs() {\n  if (!window.pywebview?.api?.get_songs) return;\n\n  backendReady = true;\n  setStatus(\"Cargando catalogo\", false);\n  try {\n    songs = normalizeBackendSongs(await window.pywebview.api.get_songs());\n    state.selectedIndex = 0;\n    state.current = 0;\n    state.userPoints = [];\n    renderSongs();\n    updateSongLabels();\n    renderChart();\n  } catch (error) {\n    setStatus(`Error: ${error}`, false);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderSongs() {\n  els.songList.innerHTML = \"\";\n\n  if (!songs.length) {\n    els.songList.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"empty-state\">\n        No hay canciones cargadas en el catalogo.\n      </div>\n    `;\n    return;\n  }\n\n  songs.forEach((song, index) => {\n    const button = document.createElement(\"button\");\n    button.className = `song-card${index === state.selectedIndex ? \" is-active\" : \"\"}`;\n    button.type = \"button\";\n    button.disabled = state.playing;\n    button.innerHTML = `\n      <div class=\"song-title\">${escapeHtml(song.title)}</div>\n      <div class=\"song-artist\">${escapeHtml(song.artist)}</div>\n      <div class=\"song-meta\">\n        <span>${formatTime(song.duration)}</span>\n        <span>${song.prepared ? \"Lista\" : \"Sin procesar\"}</span>\n      </div>\n    `;\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () => selectSong(index));\n    els.songList.appendChild(button);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction selectSong(index) {\n  if (state.playing) return;\n  state.selectedIndex = index;\n  state.current = 0;\n  state.backendCurrent = 0;\n  state.viewStart = 0;\n  state.detail = false;\n  state.userPoints = [];\n  updateSongLabels();\n  renderSongs();\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nfunction updateSongLabels() {\n  const song = currentSong();\n  resetMetrics();\n  els.chartShell.classList.remove(\"is-detail\");\n  els.fullButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  els.detailButton.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\n  els.detailButton.disabled = true;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n\n  if (!song) {\n    els.artistLabel.textContent = \"Catalogo\";\n    els.songTitle.textContent = \"Sin canciones disponibles\";\n    els.durationTime.textContent = \"0:00\";\n    els.currentTime.textContent = \"0:00\";\n    els.startButton.disabled = true;\n    setStatus(\"Agrega una cancion para comenzar\", false);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  els.artistLabel.textContent = song.artist;\n  els.songTitle.textContent = song.title;\n  els.durationTime.textContent = formatTime(song.duration);\n  els.currentTime.textContent = formatTime(state.current);\n  els.startButton.disabled = !song.prepared || !song.id;\n  setStatus(song.prepared ? \"Listo\" : \"Sin procesar\", false);\n}\n\nfunction currentSong() {\n  return songs[state.selectedIndex] || null;\n}\n\nfunction resetMetrics() {\n  els.currentNote.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.mockError.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricTight.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricLoose.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricTrend.textContent = \"--\";\n  els.metricPoints.textContent = \"--\";\n}\n\nfunction setStatus(text, recording) {\n  els.statusLabel.textContent = text;\n  els.statusDot.classList.toggle(\"is-recording\", Boolean(recording));\n}\n\nfunction escapeHtml(text) {\n  return String(text)\n    .replaceAll(\"&\", \"&amp;\")\n    .replaceAll(\"<\", \"&lt;\")\n    .replaceAll(\">\", \"&gt;\")\n    .replaceAll('\"', \"&quot;\");\n}\n\nfunction formatTime(seconds) {\n  const safe = Math.max(0, Number(seconds || 0));\n  const minutes = Math.floor(safe / 60);\n  const rest = Math.floor(safe % 60).toString().padStart(2, \"0\");\n  return `${minutes}:${rest}`;\n}\n\nfunction noteName(midi) {\n  const names = [\"C\", \"C#\", \"D\", \"D#\", \"E\", \"F\", \"F#\", \"G\", \"G#\", \"A\", \"A#\", \"B\"];\n  const rounded = Math.round(midi);\n  return `${names[((rounded % 12) + 12) % 12]}${Math.floor(rounded / 12) - 1}`;\n}\n\nfunction visibleDomain() {\n  const song = currentSong();\n  const duration = Math.max(state.viewWindow, song?.duration || state.viewWindow);\n\n  if (state.detail) {\n    return {\n      xMin: state.viewStart,\n      xMax: state.viewStart + state.viewWindow\n    };\n  }\n\n  const xMin = Math.max(\n    0,\n    Math.min(duration - state.viewWindow, state.current - state.viewWindow * 0.4)\n  );\n  return {\n    xMin,\n    xMax: xMin + state.viewWindow\n  };\n}\n\nfunction xScale(time) {\n  const domain = visibleDomain();\n  return 70 + ((time - domain.xMin) / (domain.xMax - domain.xMin)) * 1080;\n}\n\nfunction yScale(midi) {\n  return 486 - ((midi - state.yMin) / (state.yMax - state.yMin)) * 430;\n}\n\nfunction updateYDomain() {\n  if (state.detail) {\n    const center = Number(els.detailY.value || 64);\n    state.yMin = center - 7;\n    state.yMax = center + 7;\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const domain = visibleDomain();\n  const values = [];\n  currentSong()?.points.forEach(([time, midi]) => {\n    if (time >= domain.xMin && time <= domain.xMax) values.push(midi);\n  });\n  state.userPoints.forEach(([time, midi]) => {\n    if (time >= domain.xMin && time <= domain.xMax) values.push(midi);\n  });\n\n  const center = values.length ? median(values) : 64;\n  const min = values.length ? Math.min(...values, center - 5) : center - 5;\n  const max = values.length ? Math.max(...values, center + 5) : center + 5;\n  state.yMin = Math.floor(min) - 1;\n  state.yMax = Math.ceil(max) + 1;\n}\n\nfunction median(values) {\n  const sorted = [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  return sorted[Math.floor(sorted.length / 2)];\n}\n\nfunction buildPath(points) {\n  const domain = visibleDomain();\n  const visible = points.filter(([time]) => time >= domain.xMin - 0.4 && time <= domain.xMax + 0.4);\n  if (!visible.length) return \"\";\n\n  return visible\n    .map(([time, midi], index) => `${index === 0 ? \"M\" : \"L\"} ${xScale(time).toFixed(1)} ${yScale(midi).toFixed(1)}`)\n    .join(\" \");\n}\n\nfunction renderGrid() {\n  els.gridLayer.innerHTML = \"\";\n  els.noteRuler.innerHTML = \"\";\n\n  for (let midi = Math.ceil(state.yMin); midi <= Math.floor(state.yMax); midi += 1) {\n    const y = yScale(midi);\n    const line = document.createElementNS(\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\", \"line\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"class\", \"grid-line\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"x1\", \"54\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"x2\", \"1200\");\n    line.setAttribute(\"y1\", y);\n    line.setAttribute(\"y2\", y);\n    els.gridLayer.appendChild(line);\n\n    const label = document.createElement(\"span\");\n    label.textContent = noteName(midi);\n    els.noteRuler.appendChild(label);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction renderChart() {\n  updateYDomain();\n  renderGrid();\n  els.referencePath.setAttribute(\"d\", buildPath(currentSong()?.points || []));\n  els.userPath.setAttribute(\"d\", buildPath(state.userPoints));\n\n  const cursorX = xScale(state.current);\n  els.cursorLine.setAttribute(\"x1\", cursorX);\n  els.cursorLine.setAttribute(\"x2\", cursorX);\n  els.currentTime.textContent = formatTime(state.current);\n\n  const duration = Math.max(1, currentSong()?.duration || 1);\n  els.timelineFill.style.width = `${Math.min(100, (state.current / duration) * 100)}%`;\n}\n\nasync function startPlayback() {\n  const song = currentSong();\n  if (!song || state.playing) return;\n\n  state.playing = true;\n  state.detail = false;\n  state.current = 0;\n  state.backendCurrent = 0;\n  state.backendPollAt = performance.now();\n  state.sessionStartedAt = performance.now();\n  state.viewStart = 0;\n  state.userPoints = [];\n  state.lastFrame = null;\n  resetMetrics();\n  setStatus(\"Iniciando audio\", true);\n  els.startButton.disabled = true;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = false;\n  els.detailButton.disabled = true;\n  els.fullButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  els.chartShell.classList.remove(\"is-detail\");\n  renderSongs();\n\n  if (backendReady) {\n    try {\n      const response = await window.pywebview.api.start_session(song.id);\n      if (!response.ok) {\n        throw new Error(response.error || \"No se pudo iniciar la sesion.\");\n      }\n      setStatus(\"Grabando\", true);\n      startPollingBackend();\n      startAnimationLoop();\n    } catch (error) {\n      failSession(String(error.message || error));\n    }\n  } else {\n    setStatus(\"Modo demo\", true);\n    startAnimationLoop();\n  }\n}\n\nasync function requestStopPlayback() {\n  if (!state.playing) return;\n\n  if (backendReady) {\n    els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n    setStatus(\"Deteniendo\", true);\n    try {\n      await window.pywebview.api.stop_session();\n    } catch (error) {\n      failSession(String(error.message || error));\n    }\n    return;\n  }\n\n  finishDemoSession();\n}\n\nfunction startPollingBackend() {\n  stopPollingBackend();\n  state.pollId = window.setInterval(pollBackendState, 120);\n  pollBackendState();\n}\n\nfunction stopPollingBackend() {\n  if (state.pollId) {\n    window.clearInterval(state.pollId);\n    state.pollId = null;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function pollBackendState() {\n  if (!backendReady) return;\n\n  try {\n    const session = await window.pywebview.api.get_session_state();\n    applyBackendState(session);\n  } catch (error) {\n    failSession(String(error.message || error));\n  }\n}\n\nfunction applyBackendState(session) {\n  if (Array.isArray(session.pitch_points) && session.pitch_points.length) {\n    state.userPoints.push(...session.pitch_points);\n    const last = state.userPoints[state.userPoints.length - 1];\n    if (last) els.currentNote.textContent = noteName(last[1]);\n  }\n\n  if (typeof session.current === \"number\") {\n    state.backendCurrent = session.current;\n    state.backendPollAt = performance.now();\n    state.current = Math.max(state.current, session.current);\n  }\n\n  if (session.status === \"recording\") {\n    setStatus(\"Grabando\", true);\n  } else if (session.status === \"stopping\" || session.status === \"comparing\") {\n    setStatus(\"Comparando\", true);\n    els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n  } else if (session.status === \"finished\") {\n    finishBackendSession(session.result);\n  } else if (session.status === \"error\") {\n    failSession(session.error || \"Error desconocido en audio.\");\n  }\n}\n\nfunction startAnimationLoop() {\n  if (state.animationId) cancelAnimationFrame(state.animationId);\n  state.animationId = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n}\n\nfunction stopAnimationLoop() {\n  if (state.animationId) {\n    cancelAnimationFrame(state.animationId);\n    state.animationId = null;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction loop(timestamp = 0) {\n  if (!state.playing) return;\n\n  if (backendReady) {\n    const elapsedSincePoll = (performance.now() - (state.backendPollAt || performance.now())) / 1000;\n    state.current = Math.min(currentSong()?.duration || state.current, state.backendCurrent + elapsedSincePoll);\n  } else {\n    if (state.lastFrame == null) state.lastFrame = timestamp;\n    const delta = Math.min(0.08, (timestamp - state.lastFrame) / 1000);\n    state.lastFrame = timestamp;\n    state.current = Math.min(currentSong().duration, state.current + delta);\n    appendDemoUserPoint();\n    if (state.current >= currentSong().duration) {\n      finishDemoSession();\n      return;\n    }\n  }\n\n  renderChart();\n  state.animationId = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n}\n\nfunction finishBackendSession(result) {\n  state.playing = false;\n  stopAnimationLoop();\n  stopPollingBackend();\n\n  if (result?.points_ref?.length) {\n    currentSong().points = result.points_ref;\n  }\n  if (result?.points_user?.length) {\n    state.userPoints = result.points_user;\n    const last = state.userPoints[state.userPoints.length - 1];\n    if (last) state.current = last[0];\n  }\n\n  setStatus(\"Comparacion lista\", false);\n  els.startButton.disabled = !currentSong()?.prepared;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n  els.detailButton.disabled = !state.userPoints.length;\n  renderSongs();\n  renderMetrics(result || {});\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nfunction finishDemoSession() {\n  state.playing = false;\n  stopAnimationLoop();\n  setStatus(\"Demo finalizada\", false);\n  els.startButton.disabled = false;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n  els.detailButton.disabled = false;\n  renderMetrics({\n    error_prom: 42,\n    porcentaje_50: 71,\n    porcentaje_100: 91,\n    tendencia: \"estable\",\n    puntos_comparados: state.userPoints.length\n  });\n  renderSongs();\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nfunction failSession(message) {\n  state.playing = false;\n  stopAnimationLoop();\n  stopPollingBackend();\n  setStatus(`Error: ${message}`, false);\n  els.startButton.disabled = !currentSong()?.prepared;\n  els.stopButton.disabled = true;\n  els.detailButton.disabled = true;\n  renderSongs();\n}\n\nfunction renderMetrics(result) {\n  if (result.error_prom == null) {\n    els.mockError.textContent = \"--\";\n    els.metricTight.textContent = \"--\";\n    els.metricLoose.textContent = \"--\";\n    els.metricTrend.textContent = result.mensaje || \"--\";\n    els.metricPoints.textContent = \"--\";\n    return;\n  }\n\n  els.mockError.textContent = `${Number(result.error_prom).toFixed(0)}c`;\n  els.metricTight.textContent = `${Number(result.porcentaje_50 || 0).toFixed(0)}%`;\n  els.metricLoose.textContent = `${Number(result.porcentaje_100 || 0).toFixed(0)}%`;\n  els.metricTrend.textContent = result.tendencia || \"--\";\n  els.metricPoints.textContent = String(result.puntos_comparados || state.userPoints.length);\n}\n\nfunction appendDemoUserPoint() {\n  const song = currentSong();\n  const nearest = nearestReference(song.points, state.current);\n  const vibrato = Math.sin(state.current * 5.4) * 0.25;\n  const drift = Math.sin(state.current * 0.5) * 0.45;\n  const midi = nearest + vibrato + drift;\n  const last = state.userPoints[state.userPoints.length - 1];\n  if (!last || state.current - last[0] >= 0.1) {\n    state.userPoints.push([state.current, midi]);\n    els.currentNote.textContent = noteName(midi);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction nearestReference(points, time) {\n  let nearest = points[0]?.[1] || 60;\n  for (const [pointTime, midi] of points) {\n    if (pointTime <= time) nearest = midi;\n    else break;\n  }\n  return nearest;\n}\n\nfunction showDetail() {\n  if (!currentSong()) return;\n  state.detail = true;\n  els.chartShell.classList.add(\"is-detail\");\n  els.detailButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  els.fullButton.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\n  els.detailX.max = Math.max(0, currentSong().duration - state.viewWindow);\n  els.detailX.value = Math.max(0, Math.min(Number(els.detailX.max), state.current - state.viewWindow / 2));\n  els.detailY.value = Math.round((state.yMin + state.yMax) / 2);\n  state.viewStart = Number(els.detailX.value);\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nfunction showFull() {\n  state.detail = false;\n  els.chartShell.classList.remove(\"is-detail\");\n  els.detailButton.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\n  els.fullButton.classList.add(\"hidden\");\n  renderChart();\n}\n\nels.startButton.addEventListener(\"click\", startPlayback);\nels.stopButton.addEventListener(\"click\", requestStopPlayback);\nels.detailButton.addEventListener(\"click\", showDetail);\nels.fullButton.addEventListener(\"click\", showFull);\nels.detailX.addEventListener(\"input\", () => {\n  state.viewStart = Number(els.detailX.value);\n  renderChart();\n});\nels.detailY.addEventListener(\"input\", renderChart);\n\nrenderSongs();\nupdateSongLabels();\nrenderChart();\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"pywebviewready\", loadBackendSongs);\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-194", "rollout_ordinal": 1224, "created_at_ms": 1787159102324, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1224, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-194", "text": "También voy a ajustar un detalle del estado `stopping`: no debe volver a `recording` mientras está esperando que Python corte el audio y compare.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_geETDe3oFu2KVrmvo6Xhaw9J", "rollout_ordinal": 1227, "created_at_ms": 1787159103807, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1227, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_geETDe3oFu2KVrmvo6Xhaw9J", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\desktop_live.py", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -132,4 +132,2 @@\n             self._estado[\"current\"] = float(tiempo)\n-            if self._estado[\"status\"] == \"stopping\":\n-                self._estado[\"status\"] = \"recording\"\n \n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-195", "rollout_ordinal": 1234, "created_at_ms": 1787159151077, "item_type": "contextCompaction", "updated_at_ordinal": 1234, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "contextCompaction", "id": "item-195"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-196", "rollout_ordinal": 1235, "created_at_ms": 1787159159598, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1235, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-196", "text": "Retomo justo en el punto delicado: la UI “Live” sí estaba usando datos simulados para la voz. Ya la conecté al backend real; ahora voy a validar sintaxis, estados y dejar claro qué parte ya es real y qué sigue siendo prototipo.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-197", "rollout_ordinal": 1246, "created_at_ms": 1787159169224, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1246, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-197", "summary": ["**Inspecting audio/karaoke.py logic**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-198", "rollout_ordinal": 1248, "created_at_ms": 1787159175061, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1248, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-198", "text": "Vi la pieza central: ahora `desktop_live.py` ya llama a `grabar_con_instrumental`, y `ui_live/app.js` ya no usa la imitación cuando está dentro de pywebview. Me falta revisar la función de audio porque ahí es donde puede esconderse el problema de reproducción/micrófono real.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-199", "rollout_ordinal": 1259, "created_at_ms": 1787159223913, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1263, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-199", "summary": ["**Validating sounddevice.playrec channel handling**", "**Diagnosing pywebview readiness affecting audio**", "**Planning robust backend readiness detection and demo handling**", "**Refactoring app.js to remove demo and enforce backend readiness**", "**Planning backend device status reporting for mic diagnostics**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-200", "rollout_ordinal": 1265, "created_at_ms": 1787159225152, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1265, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-200", "text": "Hay dos rutas posibles: una falla real de dispositivo, o que la app haya entrado en modo maqueta porque no se conectó a `pywebview`. Para evitar confusiones, voy a quitar ese fallback visual que “cantaba” por ti y hacer que la pantalla solo permita cantar cuando el backend Python esté conectado.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-201", "rollout_ordinal": 1267, "created_at_ms": 1787159234522, "item_type": "reasoning", "updated_at_ordinal": 1268, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "reasoning", "id": "item-201", "summary": ["**Adding sounddevice import to desktop_live.py**", "**Implementing get_status with device info and planning UI patches**"], "content": []}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-202", "rollout_ordinal": 1270, "created_at_ms": 1787159235475, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1270, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-202", "text": "También voy a mostrar qué dispositivo de entrada y salida está usando Python. Eso ayuda a separar “la lógica está mal conectada” de “Windows está entregando otro micrófono/salida por defecto”.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_NhaEBbiCBtfQCWS3ikVgd6pg", "rollout_ordinal": 1273, "created_at_ms": 1787159241398, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1273, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_NhaEBbiCBtfQCWS3ikVgd6pg", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\desktop_live.py", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -5,2 +5,3 @@\n import numpy as np\n+import sounddevice as sd\n import soundfile as sf\n@@ -97,2 +98,3 @@\n     def get_status(self):\n+        entrada, salida = self._dispositivos_por_defecto()\n         return {\n@@ -101,2 +103,4 @@\n             \"ready\": True,\n+            \"input_device\": entrada,\n+            \"output_device\": salida,\n         }\n@@ -204,2 +208,22 @@\n \n+    def _dispositivos_por_defecto(self):\n+        try:\n+            default_input, default_output = sd.default.device\n+        except Exception:\n+            return \"No detectado\", \"No detectado\"\n+\n+        return (\n+            self._nombre_dispositivo(default_input),\n+            self._nombre_dispositivo(default_output),\n+        )\n+\n+    def _nombre_dispositivo(self, indice):\n+        try:\n+            if indice is None or int(indice) < 0:\n+                return \"No detectado\"\n+            dispositivo = sd.query_devices(int(indice))\n+            return dispositivo.get(\"name\", \"No detectado\")\n+        except Exception:\n+            return \"No detectado\"\n+\n \n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-203", "rollout_ordinal": 1276, "created_at_ms": 1787159244282, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1276, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-203", "text": "Primer ajuste listo: el backend ahora puede reportar el micrófono y la salida de audio que va a usar. Sigo con la UI para que deje de simular voz cuando no hay backend.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_lpug2NePdctSt8VCYFKiiwYS", "rollout_ordinal": 1279, "created_at_ms": 1787159246738, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1279, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_lpug2NePdctSt8VCYFKiiwYS", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\ui_live\\index.html", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@\n           <span>Entrada</span>\n-          <strong>Microfono principal</strong>\n+          <strong id=\"inputDeviceLabel\">Conectando</strong>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"session-row\">\n-          <span>Latencia</span>\n-          <strong>Auto</strong>\n+          <span>Salida</span>\n+          <strong id=\"outputDeviceLabel\">Conectando</strong>\n         </div>\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-204", "rollout_ordinal": 1283, "created_at_ms": 1787159249402, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1283, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-204", "text": "Ahora voy a quitar el punto que más podía engañarnos: si la ventana no encuentra el API de `pywebview`, no debe inventar notas del usuario ni parecer que está grabando.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_sabqyau1MxbqEV7qBvRhUXLl", "rollout_ordinal": 1286, "created_at_ms": 1787159256395, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1286, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_sabqyau1MxbqEV7qBvRhUXLl", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\ui_live\\app.js", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -1,18 +1,2 @@\n-const mockSongs = [\n-  {\n-    id: \"mock-1\",\n-    title: \"Contigo en la distancia\",\n-    artist: \"Luis Miguel\",\n-    duration: 192,\n-    prepared: true,\n-    points: [\n-      [0, 61], [8, 61], [12, 65], [20, 65], [25, 63], [32, 63],\n-      [38, 67], [48, 67], [54, 65], [64, 65], [72, 69], [82, 69],\n-      [90, 67], [100, 67], [110, 71], [121, 71], [130, 68], [142, 68],\n-      [152, 65], [164, 65], [174, 63], [190, 63]\n-    ]\n-  }\n-];\n-\n-let songs = [...mockSongs];\n+let songs = [];\n let backendReady = false;\n@@ -63,3 +47,5 @@\n   metricTrend: document.getElementById(\"metricTrend\"),\n-  metricPoints: document.getElementById(\"metricPoints\")\n+  metricPoints: document.getElementById(\"metricPoints\"),\n+  inputDeviceLabel: document.getElementById(\"inputDeviceLabel\"),\n+  outputDeviceLabel: document.getElementById(\"outputDeviceLabel\")\n };\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-205", "rollout_ordinal": 1290, "created_at_ms": 1787159259539, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1290, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-205", "text": "También estoy haciendo que la app se inicialice de forma más robusta: no depender solo del evento de `pywebview`, porque si ese evento se pierde la UI queda desconectada y antes caía al modo demo.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "call_3yEXPbht3xSYeMx7fWkM3mG4", "rollout_ordinal": 1293, "created_at_ms": 1787159267602, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 1293, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_3yEXPbht3xSYeMx7fWkM3mG4", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\ui_live\\app.js", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -64,4 +64,8 @@\n \n+function hasBackendApi() {\n+  return Boolean(window.pywebview?.api?.get_songs);\n+}\n+\n async function loadBackendSongs() {\n-  if (!window.pywebview?.api?.get_songs) return;\n+  if (!hasBackendApi()) return false;\n \n@@ -70,2 +74,3 @@\n   try {\n+    await loadBackendStatus();\n     songs = normalizeBackendSongs(await window.pywebview.api.get_songs());\n@@ -77,5 +82,36 @@\n     renderChart();\n+    return true;\n   } catch (error) {\n+    backendReady = false;\n     setStatus(`Error: ${error}`, false);\n+    return false;\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+async function loadBackendStatus() {\n+  if (!window.pywebview?.api?.get_status) return;\n+\n+  const status = await window.pywebview.api.get_status();\n+  els.inputDeviceLabel.textContent = status.input_device || \"No detectado\";\n+  els.outputDeviceLabel.textContent = status.output_device || \"No detectado\";\n+}\n+\n+function connectBackend(attempt = 0) {\n+  if (hasBackendApi()) {\n+    loadBackendSongs();\n+    return;\n   }\n+\n+  if (attempt < 60) {\n+    window.setTimeout(() => connectBackend(attempt + 1), 100);\n+    return;\n+  }\n+\n+  backendReady = false;\n+  songs = [];\n+  els.inputDeviceLabel.textContent = \"Backend no conectado\";\n+  els.outputDeviceLabel.textContent = \"Backend no conectado\";\n+  renderSongs();\n+  updateSongLabels();\n+  setStatus(\"Abre la app con iniciar_live.bat\", false);\n }\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019e8aa4-55db-7a22-841e-2c9a8d427c15", "turn_id": "01a01af8-8908-73a2-843e-2211c48e393f", "item_id": "item-206", "rollout_ordinal": 1297, "created_at_ms": 1787159272134, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 1297, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-206", "text": "Voy a endurecer el estado del botón “Cantar”: solo se habilitará cuando haya catálogo real y backend real. Así ya no habrá una grabación falsa disfrazada de sesión.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
